<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's health workers strike.</title>
<headline>Morocco's health workers strike.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thousands of Moroccan health workers went on strike on Wednesday, the first day of a planned 48-hour stoppage, their union said.</p>
<p>The Democratic Labour Confederation said in a statement sent to Reuters that 80 to 100 percent of staff had observed the protest in the country's most important medical centres. It said employees ensuring emergency services were not included in the tally.</p>
<p>The union said there were 3,500 doctors and 40,000 paramedical staff in the public sector. It was not clear if all were members of the union.</p>
<p>The strike was to press for a review of medical workers' status and compensation to cover professional risk, the union said.</p>
<p>The health ministry said it was watching the strike but had no figures at that point.</p>
</text>
